1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,807
OCR reads the number.

2
00:00:02,857 --> 00:00:07,950
Two Hands checks whether the whole form agrees.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,260
Gemma, on AMD, reads 23, in digits and in words.

4
00:00:13,310 --> 00:00:17,122
The rows sum to 366, not 466.

5
00:00:17,172 --> 00:00:19,536
Routed to a person.

6
00:00:19,586 --> 00:00:21,950
The paper says 123.

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,093
Every field gets a receipt.

8
00:00:25,143 --> 00:00:29,283
Verified: it proves the record is unchanged.

9
00:00:29,333 --> 00:00:32,950
Not that the reading is right.

10
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:38,078
1,270 real tally sheets, read by Gemma on AMD.

11
00:00:38,128 --> 00:00:42,694
49 capture errors, confirmed by the certified count.

12
00:00:42,744 --> 00:00:47,822
On the state's own local actas, 91.6% field match,

13
00:00:47,872 --> 00:00:52,950
where the AI tool the state bought scored 63%.

14
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:56,200
$1 per sheet audited.

15
00:00:56,250 --> 00:01:01,400
The first step: a paid shadow-mode pilot,

16
00:01:01,450 --> 00:01:05,950
on one state's count in 2027.

17
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,950
Measured, not promised.

18
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:12,450
300 random forms, chosen before any model read.

19
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:17,950
52 fields where the capture does not match the paper.

20
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:22,950
Then we tested the fix on 100 new forms.

21
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,450
Zero wrong, in 484 accepted fields.

22
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:30,950
With 95% confidence, fewer than 1 in 100.

23
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:33,354
This is the product.

24
00:01:33,404 --> 00:01:38,162
An auditor brings the typed data and the scans.

25
00:01:38,212 --> 00:01:42,488
Here, the sample: 6,000 fields, checked in seconds.

26
00:01:42,538 --> 00:01:44,892
267 disputes, strongest first.

27
00:01:44,942 --> 00:01:48,738
Each has its photo and a receipt.

28
00:01:48,788 --> 00:01:52,104
One fingerprint seals the whole report.

29
00:01:52,154 --> 00:01:55,950
Change one number, and the check fails.

30
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,450
A whole state: Colima.

31
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:03,950
Gemma on AMD read all 982 sheets for 14 cents.

32
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,236
Now a live read.

33
00:02:06,286 --> 00:02:10,807
One request to Gemma, on the AMD Token Factory.

34
00:02:10,857 --> 00:02:15,379
We cut the wait. The timer stays on screen.

35
00:02:15,429 --> 00:02:17,664
It took 90 seconds.

36
00:02:17,714 --> 00:02:19,950
Every check holds: accepted.

37
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:22,835
Arithmetic has no language.

38
00:02:22,885 --> 00:02:30,335
I filled this practice sheet by hand, in Czech and in English.

39
00:02:30,385 --> 00:02:34,950
This is a demonstration, not a measurement.

40
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:39,450
Each strong finding becomes a case in Evolus.

41
00:02:39,500 --> 00:02:45,450
The agent runs on Gemma, on AMD, and drafts the finding.

42
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:49,950
A script, not the model, scores the evidence.

43
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,950
The auditor decides.

44
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:54,750
Who pays? Mexico's preliminary counts:

45
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:58,950
INE, 32 state institutes, and their outside auditors.

46
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:04,550
On 6 June 2027, 32 local elections join the federal midterm.

47
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:08,750
The pilot runs beside the state's own capture;

48
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:11,550
nothing in its process changes.

49
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:15,283
Next: 7 more countries publish these sheets,

50
00:03:15,333 --> 00:03:19,950
and health reporting in 70+ countries runs on DHIS2.

51
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:24,238
Most paper records are private, by law or by contract:

52
00:03:24,288 --> 00:03:26,967
patient charts, loan files, drug registers,

53
00:03:27,017 --> 00:03:30,865
so nobody can publish an error rate on them.

54
00:03:30,915 --> 00:03:33,984
Mexico's tally sheets are the clearest exception:

55
00:03:34,034 --> 00:03:39,052
the photo, the keyed value and the certified count are all public.

56
00:03:39,102 --> 00:03:42,950
Elections are our proof set, not our only market.

57
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,236
Where does it fail?

58
00:03:45,286 --> 00:03:47,979
Once, the model read 3,114.

59
00:03:48,029 --> 00:03:51,636
The paper says 314. One digit added.

60
00:03:51,686 --> 00:03:54,836
The first gate would accept it.

61
00:03:54,886 --> 00:03:58,950
Gate version two sent it to a person.

62
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:00,150
Two Hands.

63
00:04:00,200 --> 00:04:03,350
Receipts for every number keyed from paper.

64
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:04,950
Running on AMD.
